# Always deploy NGMY after every task

Whenever you finish a user-facing change in this repo (Flutter `lib/`, `web/`, assets, or anything that should appear on the live app):

1. **Commit** the relevant files (unless the user said not to).
2. **Push to `main`** (`git pull --rebase origin main` then `git push origin HEAD`) so GitHub Actions runs `Deploy GitHub Pages`.
3. **Verify deploy** when possible:
   - Remote has a follow-up commit like `Deploy web build to docs/ for ngmy.org [skip ci]`, and/or
   - `https://ngmy.org/version.json` `build_number` / `deployed_at` is newer than before the push.
4. Tell the user the app was pushed and to hard-refresh / close and reopen if the phone still shows the old UI (PWA service worker cache).

Do not leave finished app work sitting only on the local machine. Deploy is part of “done.”
